WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:01.127
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.127 --> 00:00:03.232
- [Announcer] Cakes, cookies and brownies.

00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:05.651
No, we're not gonna show
you how to make them

00:00:05.651 --> 00:00:08.524
because they can be made with
ease thanks to Betty Crocker

00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:11.259
who was born in 1921 in Minnesota.

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:14.759
(bell rings)
Well, kind of.

00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:19.136
(moves into quick music)

00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:21.721
- [Announcer] In 1921, the
Washburn-Crosby Company,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:24.455
now known as General Mills,
ran a contest for people

00:00:24.455 --> 00:00:27.155
to complete a puzzle for
the most coveted prize—

00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:28.808
a pin cushion.

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:31.741
Yes, one of your very own.
(cheering)

00:00:31.741 --> 00:00:33.202
Surprisingly, a lot of people
- Ouch.

00:00:33.202 --> 00:00:34.035
wrote in to claim
(paper crumpling)

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:36.302
their prize but with a little P.S..

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.923
- How do I make my sponges?
- How much flour should I use?

00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:43.488
- [Announcer] They wanted baking advice.

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:46.299
So the customer service
department began to reply

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:48.156
and to make their tips seem more genuine

00:00:48.156 --> 00:00:50.914
they signed their letters, Betty Crocker.

00:00:50.914 --> 00:00:53.317
Betty, because it was a cheery all around

00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:57.638
American sounding name, and
Crocker after a board member.

00:00:57.638 --> 00:00:59.734
Not being a real person
didn't stop Betty Crocker

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:02.252
from having a very successful radio show,

00:01:02.252 --> 00:01:06.211
the Betty Crocker Cooking
School of the Air.

00:01:06.211 --> 00:01:08.698
With a different accent in every state.

00:01:08.698 --> 00:01:12.028
- Welcome to the Betty Crocker,
welcome to the Betty Crocker

00:01:12.028 --> 00:01:14.478
Cooking School of the Air.

00:01:14.478 --> 00:01:16.169
- [Announcer] But the
lies don't stop there,

00:01:16.169 --> 00:01:19.330
let's talk about that
added ingredient, the egg.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.545
You don't need to add a fresh
egg to powdered cake mix

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:24.853
but science says it makes us feel

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:26.328
like we aren't cheating
(finger snaps)

00:01:26.328 --> 00:01:29.478
and we're better providers.
(clapping and cheering)

00:01:29.478 --> 00:01:33.045
So thanks, Betty Crocker,
for making us all feel like

00:01:33.045 --> 00:01:37.212
we know how to bake.
(bubbles popping)

00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:40.939
(tone rings)

